      'Fixed Shrine Wardens: its troopsRemap still pointed at "Celestian Sacresants", a unit deleted in the v1.16 Celestian unification — Battle Sisters/Novitiate got correctly demoted to Elites but nothing replaced them in Troops, leaving the Troops slot empty. Now correctly remaps "Celestian Squad" to Troops. Also synced the stale codex_adeptus_sororitas/slots.ts digest (still listed the deleted Insidiants/Sacresants and was missing Dialogus and "Dogmata on Throne of Condemnation").',
      'New internal tool, scripts/sanity_sweep.ts: a static checker that imports the real production data/engine modules directly and flags structural red flags (empty option-group choices, is_character/unit_type contradictions, dangling unit-name references in archetype rules) without waiting for a player bug report. First run surfaced and fixed: Eldar Warlocks, Harlequins Death Jester/Shadowseer, Imperial Guard Crusaders, Tau Sub-Commander all had is_character:false despite unit_type saying "Character Model" (same bug shape as the Enginseer fix in GH#25); Tyranids Trygon\'s "select any number of Biomorphs" group had an empty choices list (a phrasing variant of GH#21 that the original batch fix missed); Orks Battle Fortress/Stompa\'s Supa rokkit/Grot bomm upgrades, Tau Piranha\'s Hunter-seeker missile upgrade (resolved to the existing canonical "Seeker missile" weapon profile used by other Tau vehicles), and the Horus Heresy supplement\'s Legion Leviathan Dreadnought Hunter-killer missile upgrade all had a named item + price in the header but an empty choices array (same shape as GH#24). IG Atlas Recovery Vehicle\'s unit_type/is_character mismatch was confirmed with the rules author to be stray copy-paste residue ("Character Model, Infantry" removed, it\'s a plain Vehicle). Extended the sweep with four more checks (dangling slot_to_units names — the Reiver Marines bug shape; option_group "replaces" naming a weapon not on the unit — the Myphitic Blight-Hauler "ghost weapon" bug shape; dangling variant_link references; duplicate weapon names within one unit) — all four came back clean across all 19 factions, a good sign for that part of the data\'s internal consistency.',
      'Landing page: the bottom-quote was hardcoded in Spanish regardless of the selected language, and rendered in a near-invisible dark gray — moved it into the i18n system (translated per language) and lightened its color. Also found and fixed several other hardcoded English strings ignoring the language selector: "Army Configuration"/"Loading faction data…" headings, the entire Supplements section (Horus Heresy/Escalation/Assassins card descriptions, "View Catalog" buttons), and the top tab bar (Factions/Campaign/Log in) in App.tsx, which had never been wired to the i18n system at all. Also fixed a UI bug where an announcement bullet with no natural "headline — detail" split rendered a dangling trailing "—" with nothing after it.',
      'Chaos Daemons — reported by the user via the wiki, in two parts. Khorne/Nurgle/Slaanesh-marked units had a completely empty Mark armory tab (only Tzeentch\'s existed); and worse, all 24 of those gods\' exclusive items were sitting unfiltered in the GENERAL armory tab (with the .ods\'s superscript glyph still stuck on the displayed name), meaning every Daemon unit could already buy any god\'s gifts regardless of its own Mark. Extracted the Khorne/Nurgle/Slaanesh rows from the canonical .ods\'s shared gift table into their own armory files, wired them into the loader, and stripped the 24 glyph-tagged duplicates out of general.json. Verified live: a Khorne-locked Bloodthirster now has a correctly populated "Khorne Armoury" tab and a General tab with no god-specific items left in it.',
      'Continued the wider i18n pass on the army builder itself (not just the landing page, see [[project_landing_i18n_visual_fixes_2026-06-29]]): the ArmyConfig panel ("Battle Setup"/"Army Doctrine" headers, restriction notes, Black Crusade champion picker), the unit catalogue (SlotPanel — slot names, "No units available", "[Allied]" badge), App.tsx chrome ("Build Army", "Unit Catalogue"/"Army"/"Allied Detachment" panel titles, army-name editor), the empty-roster placeholder, the Validation panel header/counts, and the whole Allied Detachment sidebar (faction picker, relationship labels/descriptions, remove-confirmation dialog) were all 100% hardcoded English regardless of the selected language. Then did the same for the three account/campaign/armory modals: AuthModal (login/register/reset-password/lost-code flows), CampaignModal (Planetary Assault create/join forms), and ArmoryModal — by far the largest, ~50 strings across every armory tab (General/Mark/Legion/Authority of the Inquisition/archetype-granted), badges (Unique/Selected/Taken by another unit/Gravis/Term), the Mixed Warband and Daemon Weapon pickers, and every empty-state/hint message. Then finished the smaller remaining pieces: ExportImport (Copy/Import Code, JSON export/import placeholders, Clear-army confirmation) and PsychicModal (Psychic/Cult Powers and Prayers/Pacts tabs, the "Always known" Smite/Legacy-power badges, and every psyker-mode explanation sentence for all_from_one/one_from_one/n_from_any). Still untranslated at that point: the individual validation messages themselves (engine/validators.ts — a much bigger separate effort) and UnitCard.tsx.',
      'Finished the i18n pass with UnitCard.tsx (2085 lines, the single largest component in the app — every other unit-facing surface is now translated): all buttons (Copy unit, Armory, Veteran, Vehicle equipment, Ammo, Traits, Powers/Prayers/Pacts), table headers (Model/Weapon/Range/Type/Abilities), badges (Trait/Mark/Rule/Option/Equip/Champion/Add-on/Favored), the Join-unit and Platoon-link dropdowns, the Traitor Guard Mark-of-Chaos cost picker, the Yngir C\'tan Shard and Gue\'vesa lasgun-swap toggles, the Black Crusade Champion toggle and its mark-bonus summary lines, and the Mark of Chaos Undivided kill-progression paragraph. ~95 new i18n keys (EN/DE/ES). Deliberately left untranslated as a small, low-traffic exception: the `MARK_BONUSES` constant\'s short per-god flavour phrases ("+1 Attack", "Tank Shock: double hit", etc.) — a nested data object rather than JSX, lower priority than everything else in the file. Overall i18n sweep total: ~260 new keys across ArmyConfig, the catalogue/army/validation/allied-detachment screens, AuthModal, CampaignModal, ArmoryModal, ExportImport, PsychicModal and UnitCard. Remaining gap: engine/validators.ts\'s dynamically-built validation messages, scoped as a separate future effort.',
